    "narrative": "Our lineup configuration for today is headlined by the trio of **Cal Raleigh** (75.80), **Will Smith** (71.81), and **Luis Arraez** (65.71), all of whom benefit significantly from favorable matchups against pitchers with elevated expected ERAs. **Cal Raleigh** stands out as the premier play; facing Mart\u00edn P\u00e9rez allows him to leverage a strong platoon advantage and a premium spot in the batting order. Similarly, **Jung Hoo Lee** and **Matt Chapman** draw massive value from the exploitable 7.05 xERA of Matt Waldron, whose profile boosts their daily efficiency scores well into the mid-60s. **Tyler Freeman** is a subtle but critical start; while he faces a tougher arm in Freddy Peralta, the +14% park factor and high probability of a stolen base against the slow delivery of the opposition make him a high-floor asset in our scarcity-driven 5x5 format.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was leaving **Taylor Ward** (48.81) out of the starting nine. While his projection was respectable, the combination of a middling matchup against Eury P\u00e9rez and a negative platoon variance tipped the optimizer in favor of players like **Jonathan Aranda** or **Masyn Winn**, who possess more favorable situational alignments. Risk management remains paramount today, as we are navigating \"Lineup Pending\" status across the board. We must remain particularly vigilant regarding **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**; despite his elite talent, he is facing Cole Ragans\u2014one of the few truly dominant arms on the slate\u2014which suppresses his score to a marginal 55.27. Keep a close watch on weather reports, specifically for any games with \"Wind Out\" designations, as these factors were the primary drivers for the late inclusion of **Bryson Stott** and **Lawrence Butler** in today\u2019s active rotation.",
